  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Scheduling",
      "items": [
        "Housekeeping reloads the configuration at most once per minute.",
        "After a failed reload, the daemon keeps running the loaded jobs.",
        "Shared pools queue jobs and DAG tasks for admission."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Clients",
      "items": [
        "The tui, mcp, pair, and job state subcommands call a running daemon over HTTP.",
        "MCP requests reach POST /mcp behind the web API's bearer-token gate.",
        "GET /metrics serves Prometheus and OpenMetrics text."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Durable state",
      "items": [
        "A state section turns on durable storage. Without one, run history stays in memory.",
        "Run history, retries, and DAG runs persist as files with atomic replacement and advisory locks.",
        "Job commands reach key-value storage, cursors, locks, artifacts, and secrets through a loopback HTTP API."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Clustering",
      "items": [
        "Clustering is opt-in. A cluster elects through gossip over mutual TLS, a Kubernetes Lease, an etcd lease, or a lease on a shared filesystem.",
        "When election is configured and no manager runs, the node skips Leader jobs and runs PreferLeader jobs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Push alerts",
      "items": [
        "A push section turns on the push service.",
        "The daemon seals each alert to a paired device's public key.",
        "The relay sees ciphertext, a device token, and a hash."
      ]
    }
  ]
